    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required `checkDigit` to be returned as a single Luhn check digit computed over the digits of the owner's `customerCode`. I implemented it following the existing Spring/MapStruct conventions:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `checkDigit` property to the `Owner` schema (integer 0\u20139, `readOnly`), placed right after `customerCode`. This generates the field on `OwnerDto`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added:\n   - A `@Mapping(target = \"checkDigit\", expression = \"java(formatCheckDigit(owner))\")` on `toOwnerDto`.\n   - A `formatCheckDigit(Owner)` default method that computes the standard Luhn check digit over the digits in `customerCode` (ignoring the non-digit city/last-name segments), returning `null` when the owner or its customer code is absent \u2014 mirroring the test's `luhn(...)` algorithm exactly.\n\n**Results:** The target test `coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode` passes, and the full `./mvnw test` run is `BUILD SUCCESS` with all tests green (0 failures, 0 errors).\n\nNote: the project working directory is not a git repository, so there were no commits to make.",
