    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe new `formatCheckDigit(Owner)` method slots cleanly into the existing family of `format*(Owner)` default methods on `OwnerMapper` and follows every established convention in the file:\n\n- It mirrors the sibling `formatMembershipNumber`, which also derives its value from `customerCode`, so deriving the check digit from the same source in the same unit is the natural home \u2014 a maintainer would expect to find it here.\n- The `@Mapping(target = \"checkDigit\", ...)` entry is placed in the same expression-based block as the other derived fields, consistent with the rest of the mapping.\n- Null-handling (`owner == null || owner.getCustomerCode() == null \u2192 null`) matches the guard style and the documented rationale pattern used by `formatMembershipNumber` and the others.\n- Javadoc density/tone matches the surrounding methods, and the self-contained Luhn loop introduces no duplication (no existing check-digit logic to reuse).\n- The OpenAPI schema addition is additive and placed adjacently to the related `customerCode`/`membershipNumber` properties with the same style (`readOnly`, title/description/example).\n\nNo class or method is becoming a catch-all here \u2014 the mapper already owns this family of DTO-derivation helpers, and this is one more of the same kind.",
